- F-34 **Against the interpreter's library, on the code of `c3b16ef2d1`, the code generator refuses 17 declarations of the fourteen components that the distance stage checks, in 5 kinds, all of them declarations that the checker passes; on the code of `d3747846c1` the count is not measured, and 12 to 14 are expected; the count can be taken only on a patched tree.** The setting is the distance stage's (F-53): the checker's failures caught per declaration, and the bound `Any`. Without the patch, the code generator stops `FortressLibrary`, `FortressBuiltin` and `FlatString` whole at the wrappers of their helper classes (row 874), so the measure's script first patches a scratch worktree (`compile-ladder/plan-31/PROBES.md` gives the patch). On `c3b16ef2d1`: 17 refused, 742 emitted, no component failure. By kind: 'Can't compile VarArgs yet' 9 (row 624); a type variable missing from the kind environment 4 (rows 822 and 812, fixed since); a closure class written twice 2 (row 315); an intersection as a receiver 1 (row 540, fixed since); and `Stream`'s `WriteStream`, whose varargs methods fail in `NamingCzar.jvmSignatureFor`, 1. The script printed 18 there, since its counter, `compile-ladder/plan-25/probes/cgkinds.py`, then counted `List`'s `ArrayList` twice; it now counts each declaration once. Each of the two repairs of those walls, measured on its own code alone, gave 15 refused in 5 kinds (`18d5b51578`, the kind environment, F-384) and, counted once, 16 in 4 kinds (`e0a5274db2`, the intersection receiver, F-386). On the code of `d3747846c1`, by reading: the 12 that neither repair reaches stand (varargs 9, the closure class 2, `WriteStream` 1); `ArrayList`, `APPCOV` and `__filter` are emitted; `app` and `__bigOperator2` pass both walls, and what stands behind them is not known. A declaration counts at its first wall, and some hold a second. The measure skips the dispatch methods, and it sees no class that is emitted and fails when it loads. No emitted class of the measure is run, and no test checks the count, since the gate's distance stage runs no code generation. So after the switch-over the code generator still stands between the library and bytecode. Each code was measured once. Command: `explorations/compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/planner/codegen-measure.sh <scratch-worktree> <out-dir>`. Detail: `compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/planner/measure-c3b16ef2d1.txt`; `compile-ladder/plan-31/PROBES.md`, "3. The measure: the declarations of the fourteen components that the code generator refuses"; `reviews/batch-33-review.md`, "3. The measure: the declarations of the one library that the code generator refuses".
