- F-352 **A compiled program has run against the interpreter's library only in a scratch tree with twelve marked hacks; on `main` the compile command reads the compiler's prelude unless `FORTRESS_LIBRARY=one` selects the one library (F-381).** In that tree, on `832f7d0d91`'s code, two lines of `Shell.useCompilerLibraries()` point the compiled path at the one library, and a one-line program then passes the checker and the code generator. Its run needs the library's fourteen components as bytecode, compiled by name in about 200 s. Three programs ran and printed walk's output: one that prints a line, one that builds and reads an `Array1`, and a dot product in the program's own loop over two `Array1`. Not run: an array of rank 2 or 3 (row 992, fixed since), the library's `DOT` and `SUM` (row 732, fixed since), and microGPT, which the checker stops (F-58). The runs met sixteen walls of two kinds. A test compiled against the prelude can show the first kind: the refusal of varargs (row 624), `label` (row 81), a closure class written twice (row 315), a method written twice (row 990), a missing cast at a `comprises` type (row 991), and rows 992 and 732; rows 81, 990, 991, 732 and 992 are fixed since, and rows 624 and 315 stand. Only a tree switched onto the one library shows the second kind: which run-time class carries each built-in type, a choice that reaches the code generator's naming (rows 874, 995 and 866); the trait table's search by the prelude's api names (row 942); the dispatch method's package (row 994); `NN32`'s two getters (row 993). Every run had the JVM's verifier off, so the number of emitted methods that the verifier refuses is not known. A program's check takes about a second under either library on warm caches, and 17 s against the one library on cold caches, one run each. Measured once; nothing of the scratch tree landed, and no test holds its runs. Detail: `compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/switch-rehearsal.md`, "2. The walls, in the order met", "4. How far each program got" and "6. The walls grouped, against PLAN's phase 4 and phase 5 lines"; `compile-ladder/plan-31/probes/model-closure-check.md`, "4. The checker's time for one program".
